% Where a decision table may be written (docs/user/reference/language.md §17.3).
%
% A table is written wherever a rule may be: as a section of its own, among the
% rules of a knowledge base (as `the table brackets is` below), or, indented
% with them, among the facts of a scenario.
%
% A table written in a SCENARIO is that scenario's, exactly as its facts are: it
% answers only while that scenario is the case, and it shadows the table of the
% same name written in the knowledge base. Here the knowledge base holds the
% brackets in force, and each year that changed them states its own — one
% program, one set of rules, a table per case.
%
% Only an indented table belongs to a scenario. One written at the margin after
% a scenario is a section of its own, a global table.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the income of *a person* is *an amount*.
    the rate for an income of *an amount* is *a rate* under table brackets.
    the tax due by *a person* is *an amount*.
    *a person* pays the top rate.

the knowledge base scenario table includes:

the tax due by a person is a tax
    if the income of the person is an income
    and the rate for an income of the income is a rate under table brackets
    and the tax is the income * the rate / 100.

the table brackets is, with first match:
    band   | income   | rate
    low    | <= 10000 | 10
    middle | <= 50000 | 20
    top    | > 50000  | 40

a person pays the top rate
    if the income of the person is an income
    and the rate for an income of the income is a rate under table brackets
    and the rate >= 40.

scenario this year is:
    the income of ann is 20000.
    the income of bob is 80000.
    tax expects answers ["the tax due by ann is 4000", "the tax due by bob is 32000"].
    top expects answers ["bob pays the top rate"].

scenario the year the top band was cut is:
    the income of ann is 20000.
    the income of bob is 80000.
    the table brackets is, with first match:
        band   | income   | rate
        low    | <= 10000 | 10
        middle | <= 50000 | 25
        top    | > 50000  | 30
    tax expects answers ["the tax due by ann is 5000", "the tax due by bob is 24000"].
    top expects answers [].

query tax is:
    the tax due by which person is which amount.

query top is:
    which person pays the top rate.
